# Member summary design candidate

## Problem

The summary currently renders `MemberDetails.summary.currencies` directly in `MemberSummary.svelte`. Its overview, counts and currency labels occupy the left chart column. `MemberIdentity` owns the name, metadata and tabs but receives no total. The API adapter already validates decimal strings and dates, and the funder/history consumers still need transport currency fields. Farage's real response has a GBP total of `2323720.45`; the employment labels span current IDs 1 and 2 and legacy ID 12. `registeredAt` is the only date available, so the weekly plot must describe registration timing.

## Usage

```svelte
<!-- EntityDetails member branch -->
{@const summary = summarizeMember(details)}
<MemberIdentity member={details.member} view={view} total={summary.total} />
{#if view === "history"}
  <MemberHistory {details} />
{:else}
  <MemberSummary {details} {summary} />
{/if}
```

`MemberIdentity` uses `formatPounds(total)` and a compact “Total declared value” label. `MemberSummary` renders `summary.categories` and `summary.earnings`, with no currency loops. The adapter returns exact values plus chart geometry; components do not classify categories, bucket dates or sum numbers.

## Shape

Prefer a local presentation module, `lib/member-summary.ts`, with one main operation. Preserve `MemberDetails` and `readMember` as the shared API contract.

```ts
export interface MemberSummary {
  total: string | null;
  categories: readonly CategoryValue[];
  earnings: EarningsSeries;
}
export interface CategoryValue {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  amount: string | null;
  incomplete: boolean;
  width: number;
  negative: boolean;
}
export interface EarningsWeek {
  start: string; // Monday UTC, YYYY-MM-DD
  amount: string | null;
  incomplete: boolean;
}
export type EarningsSeries =
  | { kind: "empty" }
  | { kind: "undated" }
  | { kind: "weeks"; weeks: readonly EarningsWeek[]; hasUndated: boolean };
export function summarizeMember(details: MemberDetails): MemberSummary;
export function formatPounds(amount: string | null): string;
```

Keep decimal arithmetic, employment recognition and Monday bucketing private in this module. Export only data that the view actually renders. Exact amounts remain strings; geometry may use bounded numbers derived from BigInt ratios. Do not convert amounts to Number before summation or formatting. An internal `{ coefficient: bigint, scale: number }` accumulator aligns arbitrary decimal scales, preserving the existing nine-decimal fixture. A fixed pence accumulator would silently violate the current transport contract.

The server GBP group remains authoritative for the top total and category amounts. Choose `currency === "GBP"` once inside `summarizeMember`. Do not add non-GBP groups together or treat their values as pounds. The outward model has no currency property. Format using the existing string grouping conventions with a pound prefix, normalize integral/trailing-zero amounts to at least two decimal places without discarding additional precision, and put minus before the pound sign.

Weekly earnings come from GBP entries in declarations classified as employment. Use the source category name as the semantic discriminator, with normalized whitespace/case and a narrow exact family: `Employment and earnings`, its ` - Ad hoc payments` and ` - Ongoing paid employment` variants, plus `Employment` if preserving the existing fixture spelling. Own these source aliases in exactly one private function, never numeric IDs alone. An unrelated category assigned ID 1 must not become earnings, and legacy ID 12 with the employment label must work. This avoids guessing the source schema from IDs; it does not claim to solve future unknown source vocabularies.

Each qualifying declaration belongs to the week containing its UTC registration instant. Clear UTC clock fields, then subtract `(getUTCDay() + 6) % 7` days. Aggregate all entries exactly; keep duplicates because they are stored funding records. Sort ascending and insert every missing Monday from the first to the last qualifying dated declaration. Missing weeks represent no recorded earnings and have exact zero; a week containing only unavailable amounts has null; a week with known and unavailable amounts has its known sum and `incomplete: true`. Negative amounts remain signed. Undated entries never enter a dated bucket. Unknown currency entries cannot supply a pound amount and should make a qualifying bucket incomplete if other GBP records establish it, without introducing currency copy in the UI.

Differentiate no earnings declarations from earnings declarations whose dates are all missing. Avoid inventing an earned date or current-week extrapolation. A single dated week renders one meaningful bar. Zero-only weeks render a baseline and explicit values rather than a zero-height empty SVG. Include dated unknown-only qualifying declarations in the period so an unavailable amount does not disappear from the time range.

## Layout and chart behavior

Put the member identity and total in a two-column header row, identity left and total right, tabs across the full width underneath. At narrow widths stack the total beneath metadata and above tabs. Place “Declared value by category” and “Earnings by registration week” side by side below the tabs. Categories use horizontal signed bars with real labels and exact amounts. The weekly chart uses bars, a visible zero baseline, signed positive/negative bounds, sparse UTC month/year ticks and exact values available to keyboard and pointer users. A nearby disclosure containing an accessible date/value table is a robust fallback for a long weekly series; the SVG itself needs a clear label and concise description. A tooltip reachable only by pointer is insufficient.

Use one short subtitle “Grouped by the week registered” if the heading is shortened to “Earnings per week”. No overview count/context block returns. An incomplete amount or missing date may need a concise chart-local state, not a replacement wall of coverage statistics. Retain recent declarations and the history link as existing navigation.

## Scope

Add `lib/member-summary.ts`, optionally `MemberEarningsChart.svelte` to keep SVG layout out of the summary template, and focused summary calculation tests. Change `EntityDetails.svelte`, `MemberIdentity.svelte`, `MemberSummary.svelte` and the relevant CSS. Remove obsolete `.member-currency-totals`, `.category-currency`, overview and coverage styling only after checking remaining callers. CSS currently defines `.member-total` twice and appends summary overrides at the bottom; consolidate these rules when changing the layout. Preserve history and funder behavior and their existing tests.

## Alternatives considered

A central API adapter could replace the member summary DTO with the presentation model inside `readMember`, then components would receive ready-to-render data without a derivation call. It hides arithmetic as well as this design but couples a shared transport boundary to page layout, complicates retention of the original currency summary, and makes route loading responsible for graph policy. It is viable if the entire member API model is intentionally redesigned, but larger than this task.

Embedding computations in `MemberSummary.svelte` minimizes file count but forces the header to compute its own total or forces callbacks/slots to push derived data upward. That splits ownership and makes weekly logic hard to exercise independently. Reject it.

Replacing API totals with a single frontend aggregation of all declarations would make reconciliation automatic, but loses the current server-authoritative total contract and breaks deliberately independent server-total tests. The local model should acknowledge the two authoritative inputs: server totals for aggregate values, full declarations for dates absent from summary.

## Verification and risks

Test the exact Farage top total `£2,323,720.45`; precision beyond Number's integer limit; Monday/Sunday boundaries and timezone offsets; a missing week; December/January; one week; all-zero and negative series; known-plus-null and null-only values; undated-only and empty declarations; duplicate entries; legacy employment ID 12 and employment labels under unfamiliar IDs; unrelated category ID 1; other currencies never relabeled pounds. Existing fixture category totals intentionally disagree with declaration records, so do not make an accidental consistency assertion against that fixture.

Check desktop header alignment, both charts and the real record at 1440px, plus 360px overflow and keyboard chart access. The week is a registration week, not a claim about when earnings occurred. No API or Rust changes are required.

## Synthesis decision

Candidate recommendation only; parent arena selects the base and grafts.

## Implementation reconciliation

No implementation performed.

## Next implementation step

Implement the pure summary projection and a fixture exercising exact weekly aggregation, then connect the same projection to the header and both charts.
